<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia Siemens opens 26 bln rph cable plant.</title>
<headline>Indonesia Siemens opens 26 bln rph cable plant.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>PT Siemens Kabel Optik said on Monday it had opened a submarine fibre optic cable factory in West Java with a total investment of 26 billion rupiah.</p>
<p>Kabel Optik is 49 percent owned by Indonesia's distribution transformer manufacturer PT Trafindo Perkasa, a unit of conglomerate PT Ometraco Corp, and 51 percent owned by Siemens AG of Germany, Ometraco said in a statement.</p>
<p>Ometraco is an Indonesian conglomerate with interests in finance, property and consumer products.</p>
<p>It did not give further details.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
